# the version DOI below (the concept DOI stays: it always resolves to the newest version).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Lite Classify, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Lite Classify"
abstract: >-
  A desktop application for geographic object-based image analysis (GEOBIA) of
  ultra-high-resolution UAS orthomosaics: SLIC segmentation, object features from RGB and
  a photogrammetric DSM, class discovery with self-supervised DINOv2 context embeddings,
  Random Forest classification, and design-based accuracy assessment.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Barua
    given-names: "L. D."
    affiliation: "Makiling Center for Mountain Ecosystems, College of Forestry and Natural Resources, University of the Philippines Los Baños"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leobarua/liteclassify"
url: "https://leobarua.github.io/liteclassify/manual/"
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23462352"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23462352"
    description: "Concept DOI: all versions of Lite Classify (resolves to the newest)"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23612117"
    description: "Version DOI: Lite Classify 1.1"
keywords:
  - GEOBIA
  - object-based image analysis
  - unmanned aerial systems
  - SLIC superpixels
  - self-supervised vision transformer
  - Random Forest
  - accuracy assessment
